From: AROS Craft ports
Subject: [PATCH] ring: AROS uses the Linux-ABI assembly and SystemRandom from getrandom

Crate: ring 0.17.14 (crates.io).
Date: 2026-11-07
Problem: ring does not know AROS. Its build script then compiles no
  assembly (the link misses the ChaCha20/AES/SHA routines) and SystemRandom
  has no implementation, so rustls (the Craft font store's HTTPS) does not
  build.
Rationale: AROS x86_64 follows the System V AMD64 calling convention and
  AROS on AArch64 AAPCS64, with ELF objects: the pregenerated ELF
  assembly fits, as for the other systems in LINUX_ABI. getrandom 0.2 is
  ring's existing random source on those systems; the Craft ports'
  getrandom patch fills it from the C library's getentropy(), which fails
  rather than returning weak bytes.
Upstream-status: local (needs getrandom upstream AROS support first).
Prerequisites: patches/crates/getrandom-0.2.17; C flags -fno-pic
  -mcmodel=large on x86_64 (scripts/craft.py), matching the Rust profile.
Limitations: the assembly addresses its constants RIP-relative across
  sections, which AROS's loader may place apart; not observed to fail.
Removal: when ring and getrandom support AROS.
---
diff --color -ru a/ring-0.17.14/build.rs b/ring-0.17.14/build.rs
--- a/build.rs	2026-11-07 09:50:30
+++ b/build.rs	2026-11-07 09:50:31
@@ -243,6 +243,8 @@
 /// mentioned in `ASM_TARGETS`.
 const LINUX_ABI: &[&str] = &[
     "android",
+    // AROS: the System V AMD64 and AAPCS64 calling conventions, ELF objects.
+    "aros",
     "dragonfly",
     "freebsd",
     "fuchsia",
diff --color -ru a/ring-0.17.14/src/rand.rs b/ring-0.17.14/src/rand.rs
--- a/src/rand.rs	2026-11-07 09:50:30
+++ b/src/rand.rs	2026-11-07 09:50:31
@@ -126,6 +126,7 @@
     all(feature = "less-safe-getrandom-espidf", target_os = "espidf"),
     target_os = "aix",
     target_os = "android",
+    target_os = "aros",
     target_os = "dragonfly",
     target_os = "freebsd",
     target_os = "fuchsia",
